From f7086ab41e650cfd363b9fe678c4361e6a3f15f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yin Li <kevinli.ai.work@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 02:00:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [KV Offload] Request-free CPU->GPU prefetch primitive

A paused agentic session's KV is stored on finish and loaded back only when a
later request's prefix lookup hits the offloaded tier, which puts the load on
that request's critical path. Measurements posted on #57103 put that at
34/65/104 ms for 4k/8k/16k prefixes on one L20 (6.4 us per prefix token), i.e.
1.2-1.4x the resume's own prefill, and show a request-free prefetch during the
tool wait recovering 52-57% of resume TTFT.

This adds the execution primitive for that, and nothing else:

  OffloadingConnector.request_free_prefetch(block_hashes, group_idx)
      -> ACCEPTED | DEFERRED | COMPLETED | UNSUPPORTED

resolve the chunk keys for a prefix -> check free GPU blocks behind a reserve
-> reserve destination blocks -> submit the existing async load -> publish the
blocks into the prefix cache on completion.

It is deliberately not a policy. The same measurements showed that "prefetch at
pause" keeps 95-100% of the oracle gain while fixed-lead and EWMA predictors
keep 5-50%, so there is no lead time and no predictor; and that under sustained
occupancy every admission policy, including one that knows the true resume
order, raised aggregate resume latency (+10..57%), so there is no ranking and
nothing is ever evicted to make room - a prefetch that does not fit behind the
reserve is DEFERRED.

Implementation notes:

- The worker side is unchanged: OffloadingWorker.submit_load() already takes a
  job id and a GPU destination spec with no request attached.
- Destination blocks are ordinary allocated blocks (ref_cnt == 1, no hash)
  while the transfer is in flight, so nothing can read a half-filled block.
- On completion they go through the new BlockPool.cache_prefetched_blocks(),
  which inserts the caller-supplied per-block hashes and then releases them via
  the existing unpin_blocks() path: readable, but last-resort eviction
  candidates. That is what makes a wrong prefetch cheap - it is evicted before
  any block a request still references.
- reset_cache() drops in-flight prefetch destinations instead of publishing
  data that may never arrive.
- Off by default: requires prefix caching plus
  extra_config["enable_request_free_prefetch"], with
  extra_config["prefetch_reserve_blocks"] as the free-block reserve.
- Three counters: prefetch_accepted, prefetch_deferred,
  prefetch_blocks_published.

Ingress is out of scope: kv_hints (#53421 / #53423) is the transport and lands
separately, so this PR exposes the primitive to in-engine callers and tests
only.

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Yin Li <kevinli.ai.work@gmail.com>
